## 4. Path with `..` and absolute path

Plan: attack `..` or an absolute path if write_file rules apply.
Bench is read plus exec check only. It does not set
`OODA_FS_WRITEDIR`. It does not write the user file.

Live:

  `bench --run ../ooda-bench/fixtures/hello.oo`
  exit 0. Prints check Nms and run Nms. No ok.

  `bench /home/jeryd/.grok/worktrees/ooda-bench/fixtures/hello.oo`
  exit 0. Prints check Nms. No ok.

That is not FAIL. A readable `.oo` path may use `..` or `/`.
`sq` keeps the path one operand to `oodac check` or `oodac run`.

`./--run` is a path (it does not start with `-`).
It is absent. Exit 2. Unreadable-file line. No run.

